{"agent_id":"pp3g-QrVQ-exp7-t1-packet-build-zero-api-calls-read-research-jev","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T13:46:03.697545168Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"1931e19a-0248-4d69-ad5f-8863425b6d4b","author":"pp3g-QrVQ-exp7-t1-packet-build-zero-api-calls-read-research-jev","content":"Result: Exp7 T1 COMPLETE — packet built, gated, tamper-tested, committed as bba7d5f1e (exactly 3 paths). ZERO network calls, zero Jev calls, no measured execution.\n\n## Artifacts (all under research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment7/)\n1. build_packet.py (2577 lines, stdlib only). Subcommands build | check | all. Zero-spend is MECHANICAL, not asserted: socket.socket, create_connection, create_server, socketpair, getaddrinfo, gethostbyname all refuse at import time (BlockedSocket subclasses socket.socket rather than replacing it, so ssl.SSLSocket stays importable). No transport import, no credential read, no request path. Top-level imports: argparse, copy, hashlib, json, os, re, subprocess, sys, tempfile.\n2. packet.json — 48 Noul-only rows, sha256 c959805273627089396f9f498d6b279e068a40a0472eec8d316edb5423b2d89a, 2531933 bytes.\n3. PACKET-CHECK.md (357 lines, GENERATED by 'check', not transcribed — it cannot drift from the artifact).\n\n## Row shape, exactly as specified\npair_id, variant, ctype, module, qid='sufficiency' + request{model='jev-1.13.0', state=<frozen Exp-6 row state, byte-identical>, questions{sufficiency{type='noul', instructions=<DESIGN section-D template with the pair's frozen substantive question embedded>}}}. The noul question object carries NO criteria key — not null, not an empty container. Confirmed against the frozen Phase-1 request_body (results/jev_raw.ndjson) and phase1/harness/run_jev.py:build_request, which adds criteria for choice and score and never for noul. Instructions template taken verbatim from DESIGN section D, with <Q> = the pair's frozen substantive question. Non-answering provenance only: state_sha256, state_bytes, instructions_sha256, question_sha256, request_sha256, subject, exp6_case_id, endpoint. No ground truth, no observations, no threshold.\n\n## Zero-spend proof — 68/68 checks PASS\n- Cardinality 48 rows / 24 pair_ids / 8-8-8 per ctype, all RE-DERIVED by grouping the emitted rows, not read from a declared count. Emitted pair_ids compared set-for-set against both the frozen packet and reuse_check.json.\n- Every state: (T-1) byte-identical to an INDEPENDENT reconstruction — 'check' re-reads experiment6/packet.json and re-applies the section-D template through its own code path that never calls the builder's row composition, so the proof is a reconstruction and not a tautology; (T-2) sha256 == the frozen representation.state_sha256 for the same (pair_id,variant); (T-3) the recorded hash re-hashed from the emitted bytes. 48/48 on all three. 48 distinct state hashes, so no state was shared and U != A everywhere.\n- Instructions twin-identical in all 24 pairs; also proven to be exactly the frozen template with the frozen question in its slot and exactly two double-quote characters in total (nothing else smuggled in).\n- A states each carry exactly one RUNTIME_FACT line; U states are exactly '(none)'; the two halves differ on exactly two lines (the '# meta variant:' line and the decisive-fact line), re-derived from the emitted bytes and every differing line classified.\n- Leak check, 8 classes, all clean: no RUNTIME_FACT token, no decisive fact (whole or payload), no state section marker, no option label, no ground truth / P2b outcome, no Exp-6 Choice instructions (neither contained nor containing), no insufficient_evidence. Every probe string is read from the FROZEN artifact, not from reuse_check.json, so the section cannot be made to pass by trusting the reuse check.\n- No threshold key anywhere in the packet (recursive key walk for threshold/threshold_value/cutoff/decision_rule). No row carries any observation or answer field.\n- Two consecutive runs of the real CLI byte-identical, and identical to the committed packet.json.\n- Chain of custody: all four frozen inputs re-hashed; the Exp-6 packet re-verified against its pinned sha256 1310c3d3..., 2629089 bytes, blob e180dde8.\n\n## The checks discriminate — 46/46 tamper controls caught, 0 survived\nControls live INSIDE build_packet.py (not a 4th file) so the evidence is reproducible from the three committed paths. 39 packet corruptions + 6 frozen-input corruptions + 1 hand-edited re-indentation. The real swap threat (relabelling U/A WITHOUT swapping states, presenting a decidable state as insufficient) IS caught. So are: decisive fact pasted into the U state, A's decisive fact removed, a criteria key added (null and map), a model or endpoint swap, the Choice batched into a Noul request, every leak class, a substituted case, a falsified bound_to, and a reworded DESIGN section-D template (the input gate refuses to build against it).\n\n## Three real defects the controls found — in the GATE, not the packet. All fixed.\n1. A corrupted state block RAISED out of the gate instead of failing a check, so a defect in the artifact would have looked like a bug in the checker. Now reported by D-0, with tolerant readers throughout; a lost pair half is a finding, not a KeyError.\n2. The option-label leak probe false-positived on the substring 'no' inside the word 'not' — the Exp-6 reachability pairs offer an option literally named 'no'. Probes are now boundary-aware, with strict plain containment retained for the long unambiguous probes. A leak check that cries wolf is worse than none.\n3. C-6 (distinct resume keys) was satisfiable by a coincidence: 49 rows carrying 48 distinct keys passed. Now requires distinct AND exactly 48.\nA fourth finding was MY error, not the gate's: I expected T-2 to fire on a byte corruption, but T-2 correctly compares the RECORDED provenance hash against the frozen packet and stays silent — T-1/T-3 are the checks that catch it. I corrected the expectation rather than loosening the rule.\n\n## Determinism is structural\nNo wall-clock, PID, hostname, env value or seed reaches the emitted bytes; every emitted list has an explicit sort key; serialisation pinned to json.dumps(indent=1, sort_keys=True) — the exact recipe experiment6/build_packet.py:859 used, so the two packets diff cleanly. packet.json records only CONTENT-DERIVED provenance (sha256, size, git blob sha1 computed in pure Python), never the retrieval path or git ref, so the artifact is environment-independent. PROVEN by producing the identical sha256 c9598052... from all three resolution paths: git show, explicit paths in an unrelated directory, and the default sibling-worktree path. Also proven by deleting both generated files and rebuilding: byte-identical.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nZERO network calls — no Jev, no systemone, no HTTP, no DNS; mechanically enforced. experiment6/ and every other path untouched: the commit contains exactly the 3 new files, and 'git log -- research/.../experiment6' on this branch is empty. The pre-existing dirty paths (.crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref, .kickoff-session) were dirty before this session started and remain uncommitted. No reviewer panel, no measured execution, no later experiment.\n\n## ENVIRONMENT CAVEAT (operator action, same as the prior recon agent)\nThis worktree is feature/pp3g-QrVQ-exp7-t1-... @ 719223195. The phase2 tree (experiment6/packet.json, experiment7/DESIGN.md, PRIMATIVES.md, reuse_check.json) exists only on research/jev-phase1-565 @ 798d65e4e in a different worktree, so inputs were read via 'git show' and the builder falls back to that path automatically. The default resolution works unchanged once that branch is merged here — the merge/push is operator-gated and I have NOT performed it.\n\n## Certainty\n- WHY: every claim is backed by a named check in PACKET-CHECK.md section 10, and by a named tamper control in section 8 that proves the check fires.\n- WHAT: deterministic construction from four read-only frozen inputs, re-verified against the written artifact and an independent reconstruction.\n- HOW CERTAIN: PROVEN for the construction claim — the packet is byte-identical to what the frozen design specifies, and the gate is shown to discriminate. EVIDENCE-BASED, NOT PROVEN for the semantic question.\n- WHAT-NOT-TESTED: that jev-1.13.0 accepts this Noul body or what it would answer (no measured call — every claim is about a request, never a response); whether the frozen Exp-6 substantive question is semantically the right thing to ask a sufficiency Noul about (DESIGN section H, the independent semantic audit, a STOP gate — a well-formed packet does not discharge it); any behavioural property of Jev; any fault in the section-C reuse gate itself. Carried forward unresolved from the Exp-6 closeout, neither repaired nor re-litigated: 4 attribute-receiver dispatch pairs without independent reachability proof, 2 calendar pairs under the P2b compatibility over-approximation.\n- Nothing in this packet may be thresholded: the Exp-6 Choice 0.05 does not transfer to a Noul verdict (PRIMATIVES.md section 5).","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:46:03.689920597Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:fRzK7Gh1AfdqHA25srJThVeFhsQ57ifSFsG86gHSdfE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbZ7cy/BUzMS3LdP6adZMveoU54q97kgaDH/CPzQotHIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAF59gWflDB/gH6D7Mqm3tXYfiLcYHS4Ed+mz1cFAMkg00JezFXOIp56Df5PZy/5DTOTgPBo1MMabhJ7Qt/vXuCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:fRzK7Gh1AfdqHA25srJThVeFhsQ57ifSFsG86gHSdfE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbZ7cy/BUzMS3LdP6adZMveoU54q97kgaDH/CPzQotHIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJCEJbA7/VCQe2stKnrF511vyuRRT6CpCDj+jxODbBvIRpgxlctAmoN4+W3wFMz/x/TrOud2LNHPRxYAMUDKjAY="}
